 - Bash: node "/private/tmp/r13/final/ours-src/bin/<tool>" --since 2026-03-29 --until 2026-04-12 --merge-identities --top 60 | grep -iE "vansh|fiona|dependabot"
FINAL ANSWER:
Two people made real commits in the 14 days up to 2026-04-12 (2026-03-29 to 2026-04-12). All figures below come from `surviving-lines --since 2026-03-29 --until 2026-04-12 --merge-identities`. They count surviving lines as non-blank lines, and also with blank lines counted.

| Person | Commits in window | Surviving lines (non-blank) | Surviving lines (with blank) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses merged) | 2 (66.7% of the window's 3) | 649 (39.0%) | 810 (40.8%) |
| Vansh Sharma | 1 (33.3%) | 1 (0.1%) | 1 (0.1%) |

- **Troy Goode:**
  - The two commits are b2005d9 "lib: annotate handlers" and 02afce3 "test: vary header coverage", both on 2026-04-10.
  - Both were made under `troy@laptop.example`, which holds 44 of the 649 lines. The other 605 lines sit under `<email redacted>`.
  - I counted the two addresses as one person because the name is the same. That is a guess from names and addresses. Nothing was written to `.mailmap`. Unmerged, the figures are 605 lines (36.4%) for `<email redacted>` and 44 for the laptop address.
- **Vansh Sharma:** commit 5317ebe, "docs: app.del() with app.delete() in README example (#411)", on 2026-04-07. One line of it survives.

I set these aside:
- **Formatting-only commit:** 62628c0, "style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", on 2026-04-12 by Fiona Formatter. It rewrote 1,016 lines in 4 files. The tool leaves it out of both the commit and line columns, and its lines go back to the earlier authors. The line figures above exclude it. Counting it would drop Troy Goode to 554 lines (33.3%).
- **Bots:** dependabot[bot] is excluded and has no commits in the window.

The tool also flagged 7 other commits that look mechanical, such as "docs: reformat license". I did not set those aside. Most are old, and none are in this window.

Surviving lines show whose code is still in the repository. They say nothing about quality or review work.

