 - Bash: git log -1 --format='%ad' --date=iso; git log --since="2026-03-29" --until="2026-04-12 23:59:59" --no-merges --pretty=format:"%h|%an|%ae|%ad|%s" --date=short --shortstat
 - Bash: git log --since="2026-03-29" --until="2026-04-12 23:59:59" --format='%h %an <%ae> | %cn' | head; echo ---; git log --format='%an <%ae>' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20; echo ---; for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 -w -M -C --line-porcelain "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -a '^author ' ; done | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -20
 - Bash: for f in $(git ls-files); do git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 -w -M -C --line-porcelain "$f" 2>/dev/null | grep -a -E '^(author|author-mail) ' | paste - - ; done | grep -E 'Troy|Vansh|Fiona' | sort | uniq -c
FINAL ANSWER:
Two people committed in the 14 days to 2026-04-12 (window 2026-03-29 to 2026-04-12) once formatting-only commits and bots are set aside.

| Person | Commits in window | Lines still in the code today |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 2 | 48 from those commits; 810 across the whole repo |
| Vansh Sharma | 1 | 1 |

- **Troy Goode:**
  - `b2005d9` "lib: annotate handlers" (2026-04-10) changed 12 lines.
  - `02afce3` "test: vary header coverage" (2026-04-10) added 36 lines.
  - All 48 lines from these two commits are still in the code.
  - Troy appears under two emails, `troy@laptop.example` and `<email redacted>`. I counted them as one person because the name is the same. Blame shows 48 lines under the laptop email and 762 under the gmail one, which gives the 810 total.
- **Vansh Sharma:** `5317ebe` (2026-04-07, PR #411) changed one README line, `app.del()` to `app.delete()`. That line is still there.

**Set aside:**
- `62628c0`, a formatting-only commit by Fiona Formatter on 2026-04-12 (+1016/−1016 across 4 files).
- Bots: no commits by dependabot[bot] fall in this window.

**How I counted lines:** I ran `git blame` on every tracked file at HEAD with the formatting commit ignored (`--ignore-rev 62628c0`). Without that, the reformat would have taken ownership of about 1,000 lines from the people who wrote them.

I didn't launch the contributor-analyzer agent or build the full dashboard (hotspots, risk flags). With only three real commits, the full dashboard wouldn't add much beyond the table above.
